# ScanBase - Development Rules

## Principles
- Keep it simple: this is a small self-hosted tool, not a platform. Prefer core Node.js features and the few existing dependencies (express, better-sqlite3, dotenv, express-rate-limit).
- Shared data: everyone who can sign in sees everything. Never add per-user filtering of scans or rules.
- Tokens never leave the server: GitHub tokens are encrypted at rest (lib/crypto.js) and only used in lib/github.js.
- Validate every input at the route level, throw HttpError (lib/utils.js) for client errors, let the central error handler in server.js format responses.

## Layout
- `server.js` - Express setup, security headers, rate limiting, error handler.
- `routes/auth.js` - GitHub OAuth, sessions, /api/me.
- `routes/api.js` - repos, scans, search.
- `routes/rules.js` - custom rules and their matches.
- `routes/github.js` - organization/repository browsing and background jobs.
- `lib/db.js` - SQLite schema (CREATE IF NOT EXISTS + ensureColumn migrations).
- `lib/github.js`, `lib/osv.js` - external API clients on native fetch with AbortSignal.timeout.
- `lib/scan.js` - scan pipeline: SBOM -> dependencies -> OSV -> custom rules -> storage.
- `lib/jobs.js` - sequential background job queue and scheduled rescans.
- `public/` - Alpine.js front end, ES modules, no build step. `app.js` wires state and methods, `js/*.js` hold the logic.
- `test/` - node:test files; `test/helpers.js` must be required first to isolate the database.

## Style
- Tabs, single quotes, semicolons, CommonJS on the server, ES modules in the browser.
- Prepared statements only. Wrap multi-statement writes in db.transaction.
- Comments explain why, not what. No decorative banners.
- Run `npm test` before committing.
